.TH GIT-@-COMMITIZEN 1 "August 2025" "GitAT v1.1.0" "Git Workflow Management Tool"
.SH NAME
git-@-commitizen \- Create conventional commits with an interactive prompt
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git @ commitizen
[\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B git @ cz
[\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The \fBcommitizen\fR command creates conventional commits with an interactive prompt. It guides users through creating commits that follow the conventional commit specification.
.PP
The command is also available as \fBcz\fR for convenience.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B commit, c [message]
Create a commit (with prompt if no message)
.TP
.B prompt
Interactive prompt for conventional commit (default)
.TP
.B init
Initialize commitizen configuration
.TP
.B config
Configure commitizen settings
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show help message
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
No additional options beyond the commands listed above.
.SH CONVENTIONAL COMMIT FORMAT
.PP
The interactive prompt guides users through creating commits that follow the conventional commit specification:
.RS
.nf
<type>[optional scope]: <description>

[optional body]

[optional footer(s)]
.fi
.RE
.SH COMMIT TYPES
.TP
.B feat
A new feature (MINOR version bump)
.TP
.B fix
A bug fix (PATCH version bump)
.TP
.B docs
Documentation only changes
.TP
.B style
Changes that do not affect the meaning of the code
.TP
.B refactor
A code change that neither fixes a bug nor adds a feature
.TP
.B perf
A code change that improves performance
.TP
.B test
Adding missing tests or correcting existing tests
.TP
.B build
Changes that affect the build system or external dependencies
.TP
.B ci
Changes to our CI configuration files and scripts
.TP
.B chore
Other changes that don't modify src or test files
.TP
.B revert
Reverts a previous commit
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Interactive commit prompt:
.RS
.nf
git @ commitizen
.fi
.RE
.PP
Commit with direct message:
.RS
.nf
git @ commitizen commit "feat: add new feature"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Initialize commitizen:
.RS
.nf
git @ commitizen init
.fi
.RE
.PP
Configure settings:
.RS
.nf
git @ commitizen config
.fi
.RE
.SH FEATURES
.PP
The commitizen command includes several features:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
Interactive prompt for guided conventional commit creation
.IP \(bu 2
Validation to ensure commit messages follow the specification
.IP \(bu 2
Special handling for breaking changes
.IP \(bu 2
Optional scope for more detailed categorization
.IP \(bu 2
Support for detailed descriptions and references
.RE
.SH BEST PRACTICES
.PP
When using the commitizen command:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
Use present tense ("add feature" not "added feature")
.IP \(bu 2
Use imperative mood ("move cursor to..." not "moves cursor to...")
.IP \(bu 2
Limit the subject line to 72 characters
.IP \(bu 2
Reference issues and pull requests in the footer
.IP \(bu 2
Mark breaking changes with "!" after the type/scope
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
.BR git-@ (1),
.BR git-@-changelog (1),
.BR git-@-rebase (1),
.BR git (1)